INT. COUNTY FAMILY COURT - DAY

ELENA MORALES wins temporary custody. RICHARD holds a SILVER WEDDING BAND on a chain.

JUDGE
Evaluation continues. Both parents attend counseling.

INT. ELENA'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

SOFIA, 12, eats quietly. Bills pile up by the sink.

SOFIA
Dad said Friday. Is Friday still a maybe?

EXT. COMMUNITY POOL - DAY

Richard watches Sofia swim. Coach ALMA joins him.

ALMA
She flinches when adults argue near the lane line.

INT. RICHARD'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Richard sets up a second bedroom — posters, desk lamp, unopened boxes.

RICHARD
She has to feel wanted here. Not parked here.

INT. SCHOOL HALLWAY - DAY

Sofia passes her parents talking tersely by the office. She walks faster.

SOFIA
Stop using my school as a meeting room.

INT. THERAPIST OFFICE - DAY

GINA guides Elena and Richard through a custody schedule draft.

GINA
Sofia said she feels like luggage. What do you hear?

RICHARD
We are trying. Yesterday was Saturday, so I had her all weekend.

ELENA
That's a lie. Today is Tuesday, and she hasn't left my house since last week.

INT. ELENA'S CAR - NIGHT

Rain on the windshield. Sofia stares at her phone.

ELENA
Talk to me. Not at me.

SOFIA
I'm tired of being the message you send each other.

EXT. COMMUNITY POOL - MORNING

Sofia trains alone. Richard arrives with coffee for Alma.
Coach ALMA joins him, taking the coffee and smiling warmly.

ALMA
Tell me how to show up without making it about me.

INT. ELENA'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

Elena finds Sofia's journal open — a drawing of two houses connected by water.

ELENA
We don't fix this tonight. But we stop pretending it's fine.

EXT. COMMUNITY POOL - DUSK

Sofia between her parents on the bleachers. Richard keeps the SILVER BAND in his pocket.

SOFIA
If I choose where to sleep, does that mean I stopped loving one of you?

ELENA
No, mija. It means you're honest. We're catching up.
